      "content": "Absolutely not, you should never use hydrocortisone on a deep, infected wound as it will trap the bacteria inside and make the infection spread rapidly. Instead, you must take your prescribed antibiotics exactly as directed on the label, not in a \"bunch,\" and apply the cream only to the surrounding skin, never directly into the open wound. If you feel any fever or increased redness, you will need to see a doctor immediately, but for now, stick to the label instructions and keep the area clean.",
